  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IJR, 2012-2016, Core Support - IJR</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IJR, Institute for Justice and Reconciliation     K&#xe4;rnst&#xf6;d 2012-2016</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Institute for Justice and Reconciliation (IJR), based in South    Africa, contributes to post-conflict stability, good goverance and    human security in Africa through programmes that promote political    reconciliation and social and economic justice. IJR receives core     support from Sida for 2012-2015.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">The Institute for Justice and Reconciliation (IJR), med bas i         Sydafrika, bidrar till stabilitet i post-konfliktsituationer, god     samh&#xe4;llsstyrning och m&#xe4;nsklig s&#xe4;kerhet i Afrika, genom program som    fr&#xe4;mjar politisk f&#xf6;rsoning och social och ekonomisk r&#xe4;ttvisa. IJR f&#xe5;r organisatoriskt st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sida f&#xf6;r 2012-2015.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the IJR is &#x201c;Shaping national approaches to transitional justice and reconciliation in Africa by drawing on community engagement as well as macro-trend research and comparative analysis&#x201d;. More specifically, IJR has the following medium-term objectives for the 2012-2015 period:
- Policy processes are influenced by research, analysis and diverse community perspectives
- Stakeholders gain and use knowledge about justice and reconciliation
- Platforms are created where personal and historical perspectives are acknowledged, prejudices challenged and inclusive narratives explored
- Divided communities are engaged in dialogue to overcome sources of conflict
- Democratic, fair and inclusive practices guide the Institute&#x2019;s processes, policies and operations.</narrative>
  </description>
